// APNT shielded pool v1: the pool settlement covenant (task 3.4).
//
// Target: protocol-design, "Settlement
// and the proof verdict", "Authorization", "Canonical encodings";
// specs/apnt-pool-settlement-custody/spec.md, "The settlement covenant checks
// an exact list".
//
// Maturity: new. Deterministic local-VM evidence only
// (packages/reference-aggregator/test/apnt_pool_settlement_covenant_v1_local_vm.test.ts).
// Not deployed, not frozen, not a chain claim.
//
// The verifier ladder emits its terminal verdict, an immutable NFT of the
// verdict category V committing SHA-256(S), under this lock. Spending it
// settles S. This script runs at input 0 only and checks, in one input, the
// seven checks of apnt-pool-settlement-custody (the pool has no deposit cap and
// no meter: historical-record, operator decision 2026-09-24):
//
//   position   this input is input 0 (a verdict spent anywhere else, for
//              example at input 2 of a fold or of another settlement, would be
//              burned), and its token is V with no capability;
//   1 statement  SHA-256(S) is the token's commitment; S starts with the
//              statement tag and this deployment's id; |S| = 88 + 314·B with
//              B ≥ 1 its u16le field (a partial record fails the split, and
//              the record count must equal B); records are in strictly
//              ascending byte-lexicographic ad order;
//   2 signatures  for every record A_k, ad_k = SHA-256("APNT-POOL-v1:action-auth"
//              ‖ deployment_id ‖ A_k), the tag-authorization message
//              m_k = SHA-256("APNT-POOL-v1:dt-auth" ‖ ad_k ‖ dt_{k,0} ‖ dt_{k,1})
//              over the record's two discovery tags (historical-record), and
//              OP_CHECKDATASIGVERIFY(sig_{k,s}, m_k, rk_{k,s}) for s = 1, 0;
//              the signature push holds exactly 144·B bytes, so no tag can be
//              stripped, truncated or appended. Order stays by ad_k; nothing
//              checks what a tag contains (its fill rule is the wallet's);
//   3 anchors  root copies are the inputs 1..C whose token is the root
//              category T with no capability, and no later input carries one;
//              each record's anchor is the commitment of one of them, the
//              copies being taken in order of each anchor's first use, so the
//              copies are exactly one per distinct anchor (no copy unused, no
//              two of one root);
//   4 nullifiers  (historical-record D2; historical-record, historical-record's measured revision; historical-record)
//              inputs C + 1 .. C + 2B are the range records, and record input
//              C + 1 + j inserts statement nullifier j (record ⌊j/2⌋, slot
//              j mod 2), κ = 2·int_le(nf_j) + 1: its token is the range
//              category with minting (RECORD_CATEGORY); its unlocking bytecode
//              is exactly the push of the record redeem <lo‖hi> OP_DROP ‖ CODE
//              (RECORD_REDEEM), CODE the range record's code rebuilt from this
//              input's lock and category, so P2SH32 makes lo‖hi the data its
//              lock commits; lo < κ < hi (KEY_ABOVE_LO, KEY_BELOW_HI); and
//              outputs M + 1 + C + 2j and M + 1 + C + 2j + 1 are its splits,
//              the data lo‖κ and κ‖hi: each the range category with minting
//              (OUT_CATEGORY), an empty commitment (OUT_COMMITMENT_EMPTY),
//              fungible amount zero (OUT_AMOUNT), the record value
//              (OUT_VALUE), under P2SH32(<data> OP_DROP ‖ CODE) (OUT_LOCK).
//              No other input (NO_STRAY_RECORD) and no other output
//              (NO_STRAY_RECORD_OUT) carries the range category, of any
//              capability;
//   5 withdrawals  for the records with withdrawal > 0, in statement order,
//              outputs 1..M: token-free, exactly the withdrawal, and
//              SHA-256(locking bytecode) = wlock_hash;
//   6 pending  (historical-record F1) output 0 is under the pending-batch lock of this
//              batch, P2SH32(<H_cm> OP_DROP ‖ PCODE) with
//              H_cm = SHA-256(cm_{1,0} ‖ cm_{1,1} ‖ … ‖ cm_{B,1}) computed here
//              from S in statement order, carries this input's token unchanged
//              (V, no capability, SHA-256(S)) and at least the fold bounty
//              P_fold; no output after the withdrawals carries V;
//   7 pool coins  Σ pool out = Σ pool in + Σ deposit − Σ withdrawal − Σ fee,
//              Σ pool in over every input after the records under the
//              pool-coin lock, Σ pool out over every output after the
//              withdrawals, outside the splits, under it, each of those
//              token-free. A withdrawal whose wlock_hash is the pool-coin
//              lock's is paid like any other: it becomes an unowned pool coin
//              (no note commits it), which only adds to the BCH the pool
//              holds.
//
// Identification without circular embedding. The range-record, root-copy and
// pool-coin locks each embed this lock, so this lock embeds none of them:
//
//   - root copies are identified by category: an input whose token is T with
//     no capability. That is sound because immutable T tokens exist only
//     under the root-copy lock: the audited genesis mints K there, the tree
//     update mints K more per fold there (COPY_LOCK), the copy covenant
//     recreates each only there (OUT_LOCK, RANK), and without a T minting
//     token (only the tree update holds one, at input 0 of a fold) no other
//     immutable T token can be created;
//   - range records likewise by the range category with minting, which exists
//     only under record locks (genesis confinement, then this covenant's own
//     split outputs, check 4); a record's data is read from its redeem, and
//     the record code CODE, like the pool-coin lock, is derived at run time
//     from this input's locking bytecode and category (RECORD_SUFFIX);
//   - the pool-coin lock is derived at run time from this input's locking
//     bytecode and category: OP_HASH256 <HASH256(PREFIX ‖ lock₀ ‖ MIDDLE ‖ V
//     ‖ TAIL)> OP_EQUAL, the pool-coin covenant's own compiled layout.
//
// This lock embeds the pending-batch redeem's code PCODE, which embeds only T.
//
// It binds statement values, never input outpoints: any copies, records and
// pool coins that satisfy the checks will do, so a settlement is rebuilt around
// concurrently spent ones with the same proof and signatures.
//
// Relies on:
//   - the ladder emitting a no-capability V token under this lock only with
//     the commitment SHA-256(S) of a proved statement (tasks 5.4, ladder);
//   - the audited genesis (task 3.2) and the other pool covenants for the
//     token confinement stated above;
//   - the range record's code (task 3.1) for the settlement authority at
//     every record input: a record is spent only beside this input at 0.
//
// Unlocking data (before the P2SH32 redeem push): <S> <sigs>, where sigs is,
// for each record k = 1..B in statement order, sig_{k,0} ‖ sig_{k,1} ‖
// dt_{k,0} ‖ dt_{k,1}: two 64-byte BCH Schnorr signatures over m_k, then the
// 8-byte discovery tags of the record's outputs 0 and 1, 144 bytes per record.
// The tags are in neither S, A nor the proof.
//
// Cost: check 4 loops over the 2B records and their 4B splits here, inside
// the budget this input's statement and signature bytes already pay for; the
// record inputs run no loop. With the moved code, this input's unlocking is
// 9,795 bytes at B = 16, and B = 17 exceeds the 10,000-byte input limit.
//
// `//@check NAME` … `//@end` mark one covenant check; the local-VM tests remove
// one at a time (replacing it with its `//@ablated` text, if any).
//
// Local VM acceptance is not chain validation, proof verification, wallet
// acceptance or spendability.

//@function 0 IS_COPY
// (i) -> (bool): input i's token is the root category T with no capability.
OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY
//@check COPY_CATEGORY
OP_DUP OP_SIZE <32> OP_MIN OP_SPLIT OP_DROP @ROOT_CATEGORY_PUSH@ OP_EQUAL
//@ablated <1>
//@end
OP_SWAP
//@check COPY_NO_CAPABILITY
OP_SIZE <32> OP_NUMEQUAL OP_NIP
//@ablated OP_DROP <1>
//@end
OP_BOOLAND

//@function 1 INSERT
// (nf i o) -> nothing: input i is the range record that inserts nf; outputs o
// and o + 1 are its splits.
OP_ROT 0x0100 OP_CAT OP_BIN2NUM OP_DUP OP_ADD OP_1ADD
// Stack: i o κ.
//@check RECORD_CATEGORY
<2> OP_PICK OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY @RANGE_CATEGORY_MINTING_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
// lo‖hi from the record's redeem: its unlocking is exactly HEAD ‖ lo‖hi ‖ OP_DROP ‖ CODE.
<2> OP_PICK OP_INPUTBYTECODE @RECORD_UNLOCKING_HEAD_LENGTH@ OP_SPLIT <66> OP_SPLIT
// Stack: i o κ head lo‖hi rest.
//@check RECORD_REDEEM
<3> OP_INVOKE OP_EQUALVERIFY
OP_SWAP @RECORD_UNLOCKING_HEAD_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@ablated OP_DROP OP_NIP
//@end
<33> OP_SPLIT
// Stack: i o κ lo hi.
//@check KEY_ABOVE_LO
OP_OVER 0x0100 OP_CAT OP_BIN2NUM <3> OP_PICK OP_LESSTHAN OP_VERIFY
//@end
//@check KEY_BELOW_HI
<2> OP_PICK OP_OVER 0x0100 OP_CAT OP_BIN2NUM OP_LESSTHAN OP_VERIFY
//@end
// The split data lo‖κ and κ‖hi, κ as 33 bytes little-endian.
<2> OP_ROLL <33> OP_NUM2BIN
OP_SWAP OP_OVER OP_SWAP OP_CAT
OP_ROT OP_ROT OP_CAT
// Stack: i o (κ‖hi) (lo‖κ).
<3> OP_PICK <3> OP_PICK <2> OP_INVOKE
OP_ROT OP_ROT OP_1ADD <2> OP_INVOKE

//@function 2 CHECK_OUT
// (data i o) -> nothing: output o is a range record (range category, minting,
// empty commitment, amount zero, the record value) under
// P2SH32(<data> OP_DROP ‖ CODE).
//@check OUT_CATEGORY
OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY @RANGE_CATEGORY_MINTING_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
//@check OUT_COMMITMENT_EMPTY
OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTTOKENCOMMITMENT OP_SIZE OP_NIP OP_NOT OP_VERIFY
//@end
//@check OUT_AMOUNT
OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTTOKENAMOUNT <0> OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
//@end
//@check OUT_VALUE
OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTVALUE @RECORD_VALUE_PUSH@ OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
//@end
OP_NIP
// Stack: data o. The expected lock: 0xaa 0x20 ‖ HASH256(push(data) ‖ OP_DROP ‖ CODE) ‖ 0x87.
OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE OP_SWAP @RECORD_DATA_HEAD_PUSH@ OP_SWAP OP_CAT <3> OP_INVOKE OP_CAT OP_HASH256 0x02aa20 OP_SWAP OP_CAT 0x0187 OP_CAT
//@check OUT_LOCK
OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@ablated OP_2DROP
//@end

//@function 3 RECORD_SUFFIX
// () -> OP_DROP ‖ CODE, CODE the range record's code rebuilt from this input's
// own lock and category: PREFIX ‖ lock₀ ‖ MIDDLE ‖ V ‖ TAIL.
@RECORD_SUFFIX_PREFIX_PUSH@ <0> OP_UTXOBYTECODE OP_CAT @RECORD_SUFFIX_MIDDLE_PUSH@ OP_CAT <0> OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY OP_CAT @RECORD_SUFFIX_TAIL_PUSH@ OP_CAT

//@main
@FUNCTION_0_PUSH@ <0> OP_DEFINE
@FUNCTION_1_PUSH@ <1> OP_DEFINE
@FUNCTION_2_PUSH@ <2> OP_DEFINE
@FUNCTION_3_PUSH@ <3> OP_DEFINE

// Stack on entry: S sigs.

// Position: the verdict is spent at input 0, and holds V with no capability.
//@check OWN_INDEX
OP_INPUTINDEX <0> OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
//@end
//@check OWN_CATEGORY
<0> OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY @VERDICT_CATEGORY_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end

// ---- 1. Statement.
OP_SWAP
// Stack: sigs S.
//@check STATEMENT_HASH
OP_DUP OP_SHA256 <0> OP_UTXOTOKENCOMMITMENT OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
<88> OP_SPLIT OP_SWAP <86> OP_SPLIT OP_BIN2NUM OP_TOALTSTACK
<54> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP
// Stack: sigs records tag‖deployment_id. Alt: B.
//@check STATEMENT_DEPLOYMENT
OP_DUP @STATEMENT_HEADER_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
<22> OP_SPLIT OP_NIP @AUTH_TAG_PUSH@ OP_SWAP OP_CAT
// Stack: sigs records authPrefix, authPrefix = "APNT-POOL-v1:action-auth" ‖ deployment_id.

// ---- 2. Signatures, record order and record count.
OP_ROT <0> OP_1SUB <0> <4> OP_PICK
// Stack: records authPrefix sigs prev k recs, prev = −1 (below every ad), k = 0.
OP_BEGIN
  <314> OP_SPLIT OP_TOALTSTACK
  OP_SWAP OP_1ADD OP_SWAP
  // Stack: records authPrefix sigs prev k A. Alt: B recs'.
  <4> OP_PICK OP_OVER OP_CAT OP_SHA256
  <4> OP_ROLL <64> OP_SPLIT <64> OP_SPLIT <16> OP_SPLIT OP_TOALTSTACK
  // Stack: records authPrefix prev k A ad sig0 sig1 dts, dts = dt0 ‖ dt1. Alt: B recs' sigs'.
  // m = SHA-256("APNT-POOL-v1:dt-auth" ‖ ad ‖ dt0 ‖ dt1), the message both owners signed.
  //@check TAG_BINDING
  @DT_AUTH_TAG_PUSH@ <4> OP_PICK OP_CAT OP_SWAP OP_CAT OP_SHA256
  //@ablated OP_DROP <2> OP_PICK
  //@end
  // Stack: records authPrefix prev k A ad sig0 sig1 m.
  OP_SWAP OP_OVER <5> OP_PICK <129> OP_SPLIT OP_NIP <33> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP
  //@check SIGNATURE_SLOT_1
  OP_CHECKDATASIGVERIFY
  //@ablated OP_2DROP OP_DROP
  //@end
  // Stack: records authPrefix prev k A ad sig0 m.
  <3> OP_PICK <96> OP_SPLIT OP_NIP <33> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP
  //@check SIGNATURE_SLOT_0
  OP_CHECKDATASIGVERIFY
  //@ablated OP_2DROP OP_DROP
  //@end
  // Stack: records authPrefix prev k A ad. ad as an unsigned big-endian integer:
  OP_NIP OP_REVERSEBYTES 0x0100 OP_CAT OP_BIN2NUM
  OP_ROT OP_OVER
  // Stack: records authPrefix k cur prev cur.
  //@check STATEMENT_ORDER
  OP_LESSTHAN OP_VERIFY
  //@ablated OP_2DROP
  //@end
  OP_SWAP OP_FROMALTSTACK OP_ROT OP_ROT OP_FROMALTSTACK
  // Stack: records authPrefix sigs' cur k recs'. Alt: B.
  OP_SIZE OP_NOT
OP_UNTIL
OP_DROP
// Stack: records authPrefix sigs prev k. Alt: B.
//@check STATEMENT_COUNT
OP_FROMALTSTACK OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
//@ablated OP_FROMALTSTACK OP_2DROP
//@end
OP_DROP
// Nothing is left of the signature push: it held exactly 144·B bytes (a short one failed a split).
//@check SIGNATURES_EXACT
OP_SIZE OP_NIP OP_NOT OP_VERIFY
//@ablated OP_DROP
//@end
OP_DROP
// Stack: records.

// ---- 3. Anchors. C = the number of leading copy inputs 1..C.
<0>
OP_BEGIN OP_1ADD OP_DUP <0> OP_INVOKE OP_NOT OP_UNTIL
OP_1SUB
<0> <2> OP_PICK
// Stack: records C p recs, p = copies used so far.
OP_BEGIN
  <314> OP_SPLIT OP_SWAP <32> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP
  // Stack: records C p recs' a. found = copies among inputs 1..p carrying a.
  <0> <0>
  <4> OP_PICK OP_OVER OP_GREATERTHAN
  OP_IF
    OP_BEGIN
      OP_DUP OP_1ADD OP_UTXOTOKENCOMMITMENT <3> OP_PICK OP_EQUAL
      OP_ROT OP_ADD OP_SWAP OP_1ADD
      OP_DUP <5> OP_PICK OP_NUMEQUAL
    OP_UNTIL
  OP_ENDIF
  OP_DROP
  OP_NOTIF
    // A new anchor: the next copy, input 1 + p, carries it.
    //@check ANCHOR_COPY
    <2> OP_PICK OP_1ADD OP_UTXOTOKENCOMMITMENT OP_OVER OP_EQUALVERIFY
    //@end
    OP_ROT OP_1ADD OP_ROT OP_ROT
  OP_ENDIF
  OP_DROP
  OP_SIZE OP_NOT
OP_UNTIL
OP_DROP
// Stack: records C p. Every copy carries some anchor, and none is left over.
//@check COPIES_EXACT
OP_OVER OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
//@ablated OP_DROP
//@end

// ---- 4 runs after 5 (the splits follow the withdrawals and the copies): keep the records.
OP_OVER OP_TOALTSTACK

// ---- 5. Withdrawals, and the sums of deposits, withdrawals and fees.
OP_SWAP <1> <0> <0> <0> <4> OP_ROLL
// Stack: C j Σwd Σdep Σfee recs, j = the next withdrawal output.
OP_BEGIN
  <314> OP_SPLIT OP_TOALTSTACK
  <258> OP_SPLIT OP_NIP <8> OP_SPLIT <8> OP_SPLIT <8> OP_SPLIT
  // Stack: C j Σwd Σdep Σfee dep8 wd8 fee8 wlock. Alt: recs'. u64le as unsigned: ‖ 0x00, then BIN2NUM.
  OP_SWAP 0x0100 OP_CAT OP_BIN2NUM <4> OP_ROLL OP_ADD OP_TOALTSTACK
  OP_ROT 0x0100 OP_CAT OP_BIN2NUM <3> OP_ROLL OP_ADD OP_TOALTSTACK
  OP_SWAP 0x0100 OP_CAT OP_BIN2NUM OP_ROT OP_OVER OP_ADD OP_TOALTSTACK
  // Stack: C j wlock wd. Alt: recs' Σfee' Σdep' Σwd'.
  OP_DUP OP_0NOTEQUAL
  OP_IF
    //@check WITHDRAWAL_VALUE
    <2> OP_PICK OP_OUTPUTVALUE OP_OVER OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
    //@end
    //@check WITHDRAWAL_LOCK
    <2> OP_PICK OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE OP_SHA256 <2> OP_PICK OP_EQUALVERIFY
    //@end
    //@check WITHDRAWAL_TOKEN_FREE
    <2> OP_PICK OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY <0> OP_EQUALVERIFY
    //@end
    OP_ROT OP_1ADD OP_ROT OP_ROT
  OP_ENDIF
  OP_2DROP
  OP_FROMALTSTACK OP_FROMALTSTACK OP_FROMALTSTACK OP_FROMALTSTACK
  OP_SIZE OP_NOT
OP_UNTIL
OP_DROP
// Stack: C j Σwd Σdep Σfee, M = j − 1.

// ---- 4. Nullifiers. Record input C + 1 + t inserts statement nullifier t; its
// splits are outputs M + 1 + C + 2t and M + 1 + C + 2t + 1, after the pending
// output, the M withdrawals and the C recreated copies (on the stack, j = M + 1).
OP_FROMALTSTACK
// Check 6's H_cm, from a copy of the records, to the alt stack.
OP_DUP <0> OP_SWAP
OP_BEGIN
  <314> OP_SPLIT OP_SWAP <162> OP_SPLIT OP_NIP <64> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP
  OP_ROT OP_SWAP OP_CAT OP_SWAP
  OP_SIZE OP_NOT
OP_UNTIL
OP_DROP OP_SHA256 OP_TOALTSTACK
<5> OP_PICK OP_1ADD
<5> OP_PICK <7> OP_PICK OP_ADD
<2> OP_ROLL
// Stack: C j Σwd Σdep Σfee i o recs, i = C + 1 and o = j + C.
OP_BEGIN
  <314> OP_SPLIT OP_SWAP
  <32> OP_SPLIT OP_NIP <32> OP_SPLIT <32> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP
  // Stack: … i o recs' nf0 nf1.
  OP_SWAP <4> OP_PICK <4> OP_PICK <1> OP_INVOKE
  <3> OP_PICK OP_1ADD <3> OP_PICK <2> OP_ADD <1> OP_INVOKE
  OP_ROT <2> OP_ADD OP_ROT <4> OP_ADD OP_ROT
  OP_SIZE OP_NOT
OP_UNTIL
OP_DROP
// Stack: C j Σwd Σdep Σfee iEnd oEnd, iEnd = C + 1 + 2B and oEnd = j + C + 4B. To the alt stack.
OP_TOALTSTACK OP_TOALTSTACK

// ---- 7. Pool coins. The pool-coin lock, derived from this input's lock and category.
@POOL_COIN_PREFIX_PUSH@ <0> OP_UTXOBYTECODE OP_CAT @POOL_COIN_MIDDLE_PUSH@ OP_CAT
<0> OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY OP_CAT @POOL_COIN_TAIL_PUSH@ OP_CAT
OP_HASH256 0x02aa20 OP_SWAP OP_CAT 0x0187 OP_CAT
// Stack: C j Σwd Σdep Σfee poolLock. Σ pool in over inputs iEnd .. n − 1 (after the records).
<0> OP_FROMALTSTACK
OP_DUP OP_TXINPUTCOUNT OP_LESSTHAN
OP_IF
  OP_BEGIN
    // No copy after the leading block.
    //@check NO_STRAY_COPY
    OP_DUP <0> OP_INVOKE OP_NOT OP_VERIFY
    //@end
    // No range-category input after the records.
    //@check NO_STRAY_RECORD
    OP_DUP OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY OP_SIZE <32> OP_MIN OP_SPLIT OP_DROP @RANGE_CATEGORY_PUSH@ OP_EQUAL OP_NOT OP_VERIFY
    //@end
    OP_DUP OP_UTXOBYTECODE <3> OP_PICK OP_EQUAL
    OP_IF
      //@check POOL_IN_EVERY
      OP_DUP OP_UTXOVALUE OP_ROT OP_ADD OP_SWAP
      //@ablated OP_OVER OP_NOT OP_IF OP_DUP OP_UTXOVALUE OP_ROT OP_ADD OP_SWAP OP_ENDIF
      //@end
    OP_ENDIF
    OP_1ADD OP_DUP OP_TXINPUTCOUNT OP_NUMEQUAL
  OP_UNTIL
OP_ENDIF
OP_DROP
// Stack: C j Σwd Σdep Σfee poolLock poolIn. expected = poolIn − Σfee + Σdep − Σwd.
<2> OP_ROLL OP_SUB <2> OP_PICK OP_ADD <3> OP_PICK OP_SUB
OP_FROMALTSTACK
<5> OP_PICK <7> OP_PICK OP_ADD
<0> <7> OP_PICK
// Stack: C j Σwd Σdep poolLock expected oEnd recStart poolOut o, o from j = M + 1; the splits are
// outputs recStart .. oEnd − 1, recStart = j + C, which check 4 has read.
OP_TXOUTPUTCOUNT OP_OVER OP_GREATERTHAN
OP_IF
  OP_BEGIN
    OP_DUP <3> OP_PICK <5> OP_PICK OP_WITHIN OP_NOT
    OP_IF
      OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY
      // 6. No output after the withdrawals carries the verdict category.
      //@check NO_OTHER_VERDICT
      OP_DUP OP_SIZE <32> OP_MIN OP_SPLIT OP_DROP <0> OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY OP_EQUAL OP_NOT OP_VERIFY
      //@end
      // No range-category output outside the splits.
      //@check NO_STRAY_RECORD_OUT
      OP_DUP OP_SIZE <32> OP_MIN OP_SPLIT OP_DROP @RANGE_CATEGORY_PUSH@ OP_EQUAL OP_NOT OP_VERIFY
      //@end
      OP_OVER OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE <7> OP_PICK OP_EQUAL
      OP_IF
        //@check POOL_OUT_TOKEN_FREE
        OP_DUP <0> OP_EQUALVERIFY
        //@end
        OP_OVER OP_OUTPUTVALUE <3> OP_ROLL OP_ADD OP_ROT OP_ROT
      OP_ENDIF
      OP_DROP
    OP_ENDIF
    OP_1ADD OP_DUP OP_TXOUTPUTCOUNT OP_NUMEQUAL
  OP_UNTIL
OP_ENDIF
OP_DROP
OP_ROT OP_ROT OP_2DROP
// Stack: C j Σwd Σdep poolLock expected poolOut.
//@check POOL_SUM
OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
//@ablated OP_2DROP
//@end
OP_DROP

// ---- 6. The pending output, under P2SH32(<H_cm> OP_DROP ‖ PCODE).
<0> OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE @PENDING_HEAD_PUSH@ OP_FROMALTSTACK OP_CAT @PENDING_TAIL_PUSH@ OP_CAT OP_HASH256 0x02aa20 OP_SWAP OP_CAT 0x0187 OP_CAT
//@check PENDING_LOCK
OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@ablated OP_2DROP
//@end
//@check PENDING_CATEGORY
<0> OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY <0> OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
//@check PENDING_COMMITMENT
<0> OP_OUTPUTTOKENCOMMITMENT <0> OP_UTXOTOKENCOMMITMENT OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
//@check PENDING_VALUE
<0> OP_OUTPUTVALUE @FOLD_BOUNTY_PUSH@ OP_GREATERTHANOREQUAL OP_VERIFY
//@end

OP_2DROP OP_2DROP <1>
